## HR Attrition Analysis — Dataset

## Overview

This folder documents the dataset used in the HR Attrition Analysis project.

## Dataset Source

The project uses the IBM HR Analytics Employee Attrition dataset, a commonly used dataset for exploring workforce 
characteristics and employee attrition.

## Dataset Overview

The dataset contains 1,470 employee records and 35 attributes describing employee demographics, job characteristics, 
compensation, work conditions, and attrition status.

## Analytical Focus

The dataset was used to investigate:

Employee attrition across departments.
The relationship between overtime and attrition.
Attrition patterns among employees with shorter tenure.
Differences in monthly income between employees who left and those who stayed.

## Data Preparation

The data was reviewed and prepared for analysis. SQL and Python were used for analytical work, including statistical testing.

Data Privacy and Usage

Only datasets that are permitted for redistribution should be uploaded to this repository. If the dataset is not included, 
this README documents its source and role in the project.

## Key Takeaway

A clearly documented dataset supports transparency, reproducibility, and reliable interpretation of analytical findings.
